Two-weaponing Grimtooth is quite adequate for the wimpy Master
Assasin. Personally, I think the best weapons for rogues are Magicbane
and Grayswandir. If you're able to clear the castle with your current
materials, I'd wait on altar-camping and wish for one of these.
Alternatively, if you altar camp, settle for nothing less than Frosty
or Stormy.

> And one more. Without "protection from shape changer" the rogue's quest
> seems quite dangerous; would you spend a wish on that ring?
>

It is risky. But rather than the ring, I'd wish for magic resistance
or reflection instead, which should offer adequate protection from an
ephemeral arch-lich or black dragon. If you're really worried, then
dig down to the master's level and use confused/cursed teleportation
to escape if you land in the wrong spot.
Personally, I'd be more worried about the guardian nagas. Wear free
action if you have it, otherwise stay the hell away from them.

Alternatively, genocide chameleons. :)



